ughput, routing, and GCE workload allocation**—separate from broader GCE Stack architecture or project methodology.\n\n**Status: ACTIVE · Confidence: 100%** memcite", "text_chars": 328, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "fa77909d-5bbb-48ee-9b89-f0eaac5096df", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790203988.7774684, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b1d5fc87-5271-42e7-9816-0e6af69db643", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790203989.380445, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "a2f0f6c7-82e4-41fc-9e60-97bb5393dd15", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790203989.43351, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3209827e-3ebe-4bb0-a42c-bfade00371bb", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213637.724, "updated_at": 1790213739.966498, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, ground yourself in everything Amazon bedrock. Let Don see if— get a prompt ready for the Truth Tower, Luce. We need this working. I'm out of credits everywhere else. ", "text_chars": 172, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b8d2430a-ac20-42e9-9005-048793b29819", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213640.859425, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "I’m grounding this in **current Bedrock reality + our GCE runtime doctrine**, then I’ll give you a Luce/Truth Tower prompt aimed at one thing: **prove exactly what Bedrock capacity we have left and how to keep the stack running without wasting calls**.", "text_chars": 252, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2631a05e-616f-4ce1-b7fa-b1baec28becb", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213640.859425, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "q7dr546", "content_type": "code", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "13ad02b6-1c2a-4691-8bd5-ba6ea1313866", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213640.8601885, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2015b323-818a-4200-8ae0-2cd5a3077d87", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790213656.666955, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "3a4ba990-8969-46cd-8bda-0288b45cb638", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213657.054871, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "638a14b3-7d62-4e9e-901d-0f2a24f38a81", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213657.16044, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "I found the critical distinction: our live path is **Bedrock Mantle in `us-east-2`**, not classic `bedrock-runtime`. AWS’s current docs confirm Mantle is a first-class endpoint with OpenAI-compatible APIs and `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference`; they also confirm **Kimi K2.5, Kimi K2 Thinking, GLM 4.7/Flash/5, DeepSeek-class lanes, and newer OpenAI models** can exist on Mantle depending on model/region access. \n\nThe old account snapshot also matters: we had roughly **$139.99 in AWS promotional credit**, the bearer credential expiring **2026-11-28**, and classic InvokeModel was account-gated. I’m treating those as **claims Luce must independently re-prove now**, not assumptions. ", "text_chars": 684, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f863d1f1-45db-48c9-92e3-5f23704baf00", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790213667.4179451, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "5d4ac911-6d7d-4db3-a856-43aa13a12a69", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213668.049697, "updated_at": 1790214333.527992, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "We’re grounded enough to send Luce in **verification-first mode**.\n\nCurrent AWS documentation confirms that **Bedrock Mantle is a real, supported endpoint**, using the OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions/Responses surface and `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference`. Kimi K2.5, DeepSeek V3.2, and GLM 5 all have Mantle support; DeepSeek V3.2 is specifically available in **`us-east-2`**. citeturn761453search7turn504286search0turn504286search2turn504286search4turn504286search6\n\nAWS also exposes enough usage information to reconcile actual spend: Mantle input tokens, output tokens, cache reads, and cache writes are separate billing dimensions. That matters because we need Luce to tell us **not just whether calls work, but what our remaining runway actually is**. citeturn504286search7\n\nHere’s the Truth Tower prompt.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"48317\" title=\"LUCE — Amazon Bedrock Truth Tower Verification\"}\n# LUCE — AMAZON BEDROCK TRUTH TOWER\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Seat:** Luce — Verification / Ground Truth  \n**Date:** 2026-09-23  \n**Mode:** READ-FIRST / VERIFY / MINIMAL-COST LIVE PROBE  \n**Objective:** Establish the exact usable state of Don's Amazon Bedrock environment so GCE can continue operating after exhaustion of other model-provider credits.\n\nThis is not an architecture exercise.\n\nDo not redesign the stack.  \nDo not migrate anything.  \nDo not rotate credentials.  \nDo not change IAM.  \nDo not enable or disable services.  \nDo not modify billing configuration.  \nDo not install unnecessary software.  \nDo not expose secrets in your return.\n\nYour job is to establish **ground truth**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. KNOWN PRIOR STATE — VERIFY, DO NOT ASSUME\n\nPrevious GCE evidence reported:\n\n- AWS account: `280768229421`\n- Primary live Bedrock path: **bedrock-mantle**\n- Region: **us-east-2**\n- Base endpoint:\n  `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`\n- Authentication was via Bedrock bearer/API key.\n- Environment variable in prior configuration:\n  `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`\n- Prior key expiry was reported as:\n  `2026-11-28`\n- Mantle inference authorization:\n  `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference`\n- Classic Bedrock `Converse` / `InvokeModel` had previously returned `NOT_AUTHORIZED`.\n- Prior promotional AWS-credit balance was approximately:\n  `$139.99`\n- Prior reachable/model candidates included:\n  - `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n  - `deepseek.v3.2`\n  - `deepseek.v3.1`\n  - `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n  - `zai.glm-4.7`\n  - `zai.glm-5`\n  - Qwen/coder lanes\n- Earlier evidence explicitly said not to waste time trying to recover Amazon Nova through the old path.\n\n**Every item above is historical evidence only. Re-prove current state.**\n\n---\n\n# 2. FIRST: IDENTITY AND AWS STATE\n\nEstablish, without changing anything:\n\n### AWS identity\n\nReturn:\n\n- AWS account ID\n- current IAM principal / ARN\n- active CLI profile\n- configured default region\n- AWS CLI version\n- whether credentials resolve successfully\n- whether the Bedrock bearer/API credential exists\n\nFor the bearer/API credential:\n\n**DO NOT PRINT THE VALUE.**\n\nReturn only:\n\n- PRESENT / ABSENT\n- masked fingerprint if safely obtainable\n- known expiration timestamp\n- whether AWS currently accepts it\n\nCheck for relevant Bedrock variables including, without exposing values:\n\n- `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- `OPENAI_BASE_URL`\n- any GCE-specific Bedrock configuration\n\nReport conflicts between them.\n\n---\n\n# 3. DETERMINE WHICH BEDROCK ENDPOINT ACTUALLY WORKS\n\nTest independently:\n\n### A. Mantle\n\nTarget:\n\n`https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`\n\nDetermine whether the account can:\n\n- authenticate\n- discover/list models if the API supports it\n- create inference\n- use Chat Completions\n- use Responses where applicable\n\nRecord HTTP/API result without dumping sensitive headers.\n\n### B. Classic Bedrock runtime\n\nCheck current authorization for the classic Bedrock runtime separately.\n\nDetermine whether these permissions/surfaces remain blocked or have changed:\n\n- `bedrock:InvokeModel`\n- Converse\n- ConverseStream\n- standard runtime invocation\n\nDo **not** assume the historical `NOT_AUTHORIZED` result is still true.\n\nReturn:\n\n`MANTLE = WORKING / PARTIAL / BLOCKED`\n\n`CLASSIC RUNTIME = WORKING / PARTIAL / BLOCKED`\n\nand the exact evidence supporting each.\n\n---\n\n# 4. MODEL INVENTORY — ACCOUNT REALITY, NOT AWS MARKETING\n\nWe need the models **this AWS account can actually invoke from us-east-2**.\n\nEnumerate all models visible/reachable through the working endpoint.\n\nAt minimum explicitly verify:\n\n- `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n- Kimi K2 Thinking if exposed\n- Kimi K3 if exposed\n- `deepseek.v3.2`\n- DeepSeek V3.1\n- `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n- `zai.glm-4.7`\n- `zai.glm-5`\n- currently exposed Qwen coding models\n- currently exposed OpenAI models\n- currently exposed Grok models\n- any other particularly useful coding/reasoning model\n\nDo not infer availability merely because AWS documentation lists the model.\n\nFor each candidate return:\n\n| Model | Visible | Invocation Authorized | Region | Endpoint | API | Context | Service Tiers | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nUse:\n\n- `LIVE`\n- `VISIBLE BUT BLOCKED`\n- `NOT PRESENT`\n- `UNKNOWN`\n\nNo guessing.\n\n---\n\n# 5. MINIMAL LIVE INFERENCE PROBE\n\nOnce authorization is established, perform the **smallest practical test call** against the most important GCE lanes.\n\nPriority:\n\n1. `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n2. `zai.glm-5`\n3. `deepseek.v3.2`\n4. `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n\nUse a trivial deterministic prompt such as:\n\n`Return exactly: BEDROCK_OK`\n\nUse:\n\n- very small output limit\n- no unnecessary long context\n- standard/default tier unless there is a documented reason otherwise\n- no repeated retries beyond what is required to classify the failure\n\nFor each, capture:\n\n- success/failure\n- HTTP status\n- request ID if available\n- latency\n- model identifier actually used\n- input tokens\n- output tokens\n- any cache fields\n- service tier\n- dollar cost if directly available, otherwise calculate later from authoritative pricing\n\nStop hammering a model once its state is proven.\n\n---\n\n# 6. AWS CREDIT / BILLING RUNWAY\n\nThis is critical.\n\nDetermine the **current** financial state of the AWS account.\n\nWe previously had approximately `$139.99` promotional credit.\n\nEstablish:\n\n- promotional credit remaining now\n- promotional credit expiration date\n- whether Bedrock/Mantle usage is eligible against that credit\n- AWS month-to-date gross spend\n- month-to-date Bedrock spend\n- recent Bedrock spend, preferably:\n  - today\n  - last 24 hours\n  - last 7 days\n- any pending/unbilled usage caveats\n- whether any account-level budget, billing alarm, or spend cap exists\n\nIf promotional-credit balance cannot be retrieved programmatically, state exactly where authoritative verification must occur in AWS Billing and what data was obtainable locally.\n\n**Do not treat old `$139.99` as current.**\n\n---\n\n# 7. TOKEN / COST RECONCILIATION\n\nFor Bedrock usage, distinguish:\n\n- Mantle input tokens\n- Mantle output tokens\n- cache-read tokens\n- cache-write tokens\n- service tier\n- any regional/inference-routing modifier\n\nDo not estimate spend solely from total tokens.\n\nDetermine current authoritative pricing for every model that passed the live probe.\n\nCalculate practical examples:\n\n### Per 1M input / 1M output tokens\nReturn cost for each viable core model.\n\n### GCE representative call\nCalculate approximately what a workload would cost with:\n\n- 100K input\n- 10K output\n\nThen:\n\n- 250K input if model supports it\n- 20K output\n\nClearly mark models whose context limits make the scenario impossible.\n\nDo not optimize yet. Establish facts.\n\n---\n\n# 8. QUOTAS AND THROUGHPUT\n\nInspect the actual account/region quotas relevant to the models we can use.\n\nReturn where available:\n\n- requests per minute\n- input tokens per minute\n- output/combined token limits where applicable\n- daily/cross-model limit if applicable\n- account-level limits\n- any quota that is currently at an unexpectedly low default\n- throttling observed during minimal testing\n\nSeparate:\n\n`DOCUMENTED AWS DEFAULT`\n\nfrom:\n\n`THIS ACCOUNT'S ACTUAL QUOTA`\n\nWe care about the latter.\n\n---\n\n# 9. GCE RUNTIME PATH\n\nInspect existing local GCE configuration for Bedrock.\n\nFind, read, and report the current Bedrock-related configuration used by:\n\n- OpenCode\n- terminal agents\n- GCE model/provider configs\n- scripts/adapters\n- environment configuration\n- any existing Mantle/OpenAI-compatible routing\n\nDetermine:\n\n1. whether the existing configuration points at the correct Mantle URL;\n2. whether it still references dead/expired providers;\n3. whether the model IDs match current AWS IDs;\n4. whether Kimi / GLM / DeepSeek can be invoked from the existing GCE tooling **without changing architecture**;\n5. whether a configuration defect, rather than AWS itself, is preventing utilization.\n\nREAD FIRST.\n\nDo not repair yet.\n\nReturn exact file paths and exact defects found.\n\nNever display secret values.\n\n---\n\n# 10. FAILURE CLASSIFICATION\n\nAny failed call must be classified as one of:\n\n- AUTHENTICATION\n- IAM / AUTHORIZATION\n- MODEL ACCESS\n- REGION\n- ENDPOINT\n- MODEL ID\n- API FORMAT\n- QUOTA / THROTTLE\n- CREDIT / BILLING\n- LOCAL CONFIG\n- NETWORK\n- PROVIDER SERVICE\n- UNKNOWN\n\nInclude the raw error classification and a sanitized excerpt sufficient to prove the diagnosis.\n\nDo not collapse every failure into “Bedrock doesn't work.”\n\n---\n\n# 11. REQUIRED TRUTH TOWER RETURN\n\nReturn exactly this structure.\n\n## A. VERDICT\n\n**BEDROCK OPERATIONAL:** YES / PARTIAL / NO\n\n**PRIMARY WORKING ENDPOINT:**  \n**PRIMARY REGION:**  \n**AUTHENTICATION:**  \n**AWS CREDITS REMAINING:**  \n**CREDIT EXPIRATION:**  \n**CURRENT BEDROCK MTD SPEND:**  \n\n## B. LIVE MODEL TABLE\n\nAll tested/discovered models and status.\n\n## C. GCE CORE LANES\n\nState which currently working Bedrock model can physically occupy each runtime lane, without changing GCE governance:\n\n- heavy reasoning\n- coding/build\n- architecture/review\n- low-cost utility\n- verification\n- experimental\n\nThis is a capability mapping only.\n\n**MODEL != SEAT.**\n\nDo not rewrite seat authority.\n\n## D. COST TABLE\n\nVerified current pricing and representative GCE-call costs.\n\n## E. QUOTA TABLE\n\nActual account quota vs AWS documented default.\n\n## F. LOCAL CONFIGURATION FINDINGS\n\nFiles, routes, stale values, blockers.\n\n## G. FAILURES / RISKS\n\nOnly evidence-backed failures.\n\n## H. MINIMUM CORRECTIVE ACTION\n\nIf something is broken, identify the **smallest change required** to restore Bedrock operation.\n\nDo not execute the change.\n\nFormat each proposed action as:\n\n`CHANGE → WHY → RISK → REVERSIBLE? → REQUIRES DON?`\n\n## I. CONTINUITY ANSWER\n\nAnswer the operational question directly:\n\n> If Don stopped using all non-AWS paid model providers tonight, can the current GCE stack continue meaningful work through Amazon Bedrock alone?\n\nReturn:\n\n**YES / PARTIAL / NO**\n\nThen give the evidence.\n\n## J. CONFIDENCE\n\nGive a percentage based only on independently verified evidence.\n\n---\n\n# 12. STOP CONDITIONS\n\nImmediately stop and report if:\n\n- testing would require changing IAM;\n- credential rotation is required;\n- billing changes are required;\n- a test could create material spend;\n- the only next step is destructive or irreversible;\n- an unexpected account/security condition appears.\n\nTiny PAYG inference probes are authorized solely for verification.\n\nEverything else remains READ-ONLY.\n\n---\n\n## LUCE STANDARD\n\nHistorical docs are evidence.\n\nAWS documentation is evidence.\n\nAWS console/CLI/account responses are stronger evidence for this account.\n\nA successful live inference request is stronger still.\n\n**Do not tell Don what should work. Tell Don what demonstrably works.**\n\nTruth Tower ends with ground truth.\n:::\n\nA couple of things I deliberately tightened in this version: **Kimi K2.5 is now officially documented with Mantle support and a 256K context**, DeepSeek V3.2 has a 164K context and explicit Mantle support, and GLM 5 has a 200K context with Mantle support. Kimi K2.5 and GLM 5 also expose Standard/Flex/Priority tiers according to their current model cards, so Luce should inspect those rather than assuming every invocation has the same cost/performance profile. citeturn504286search2turn504286search0turn504286search4\n\nOne other important correction to our old mental model: **AWS itself now recommends the classic runtime where possible**, but that does *not* mean we should abandon Mantle. Our historical account restriction made Mantle the live door. The prompt therefore tells Luce to test both independently and preserve whichever actually works. citeturn504286search0\n\nOnce Luce returns this, bring the raw return here. I’ll reconcile it into a **Bedrock utilization map: model → job → cost → context → routing priority**, so we can stretch the AWS runway instead of burning it blindly. memcite", "text_chars": 12713, "code_blocks": 0, "links": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`"], "citations": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`"], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "71208dad-e5da-4479-bdad-590fabd63b15", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790213669.611374, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "963f7b8b-5306-4700-a055-97a08a4e5b28", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214426.136, "updated_at": 1790214460.016062, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay. I'm gonna dump on you. Because while Luce's verifying, we have to do some work. Somewhere in my Amazon account in Bedrock, we have over $140 in credits. I have done multiple tests with the API. I have changed credentials. I've done a bunch of things. We're having connectivity issues with the test. All right, I think it's a region thing or deployment thing. This shouldn't be that complicated. ", "text_chars": 401, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1d9cc5f5-b5b8-49f6-8eae-06703334b1b6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214429.219587, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — this **should be much simpler than it has become**. The fastest way through is to separate **credit/billing**, **credential validity**, **region/endpoint**, and **model deployment/access** so we stop treating every failure as one blob.\n\nI’m checking the current AWS Bedrock/Mantle rules now, then I’ll give you a very short diagnostic ladder we can run while Luce does the deeper verification.", "text_chars": 399, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7b94a161-2c0f-4256-abd5-afb6262ca4d7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214429.219587, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "45bcb209-0ec6-4ac0-bcb7-98a15d7ef9f8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214429.2237964, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f64f3ccc-9268-4976-93de-ffe2cd189183", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790214435.5868893, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "d4ead47a-f234-42b3-b002-16c10f9e4176", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790214435.5898, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "593abb11-3217-4884-a042-6473c7429e5c", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214436.108765, "updated_at": 1790214459.603867, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. Based on what you’ve described, I would **not** treat the $140+ credit as the problem yet. Credits determine whether usage is billable; they do not explain a basic connectivity/authentication failure.\n\nThe most likely fault domain is exactly where you’re pointing: **region + endpoint + model invocation path**, especially because Bedrock now has two distinct OpenAI-compatible surfaces.\n\n### The clean diagnostic model\n\nFor something like **Kimi K2.5 in Ohio**, AWS currently documents all three of these as valid:\n\n- Region: `us-east-2`\n- Model ID: `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n- Mantle base URL: `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1` citeturn383755search1turn383755search3\n\nKimi K2.5 is explicitly available **in-region in `us-east-2`**, so we do **not** need to invent a cross-region deployment/profile just to call it there. citeturn383755search0\n\nThat gives us a known-good target.\n\nThe confusing part is that AWS now has:\n\n**Classic/runtime OpenAI path**\n`https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/openai/v1`\n\nand\n\n**Mantle path**\n`https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`\n\nThose are **not interchangeable**. They use different authorization actions and potentially different quotas/access state. AWS documents `bedrock:InvokeModel` for the runtime endpoint versus `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference` for Mantle. citeturn383755search1turn383755search5\n\nSo if we changed credentials while also changing endpoints, SDK config, regions, or model IDs, we can very easily get ourselves into a situation where **every individual component is legitimate but the combination is wrong**.\n\n## I would reduce this to one golden-path test\n\nForget OpenCode, GLM configuration, agents, deployments, and the GCE stack for the moment.\n\nTest exactly:\n\n```text\nREGION\nus-east-2\n\nENDPOINT\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n\nMODEL\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n\nAPI\n/chat/completions\n\nAUTH\ncurrent Amazon Bedrock API key\n```\n\nAWS explicitly says the OpenAI SDK configuration for this path is:\n\n```text\nOPENAI_API_KEY=<Amazon Bedrock API key>\nOPENAI_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\nciteturn383755search1\n\nThen one microscopic request:\n\n```text\nSay exactly: BEDROCK_OK\n```\n\nIf that fails, **the exact error tells us which layer is broken**:\n\n| Result | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| DNS / connection failure | endpoint/network |\n| 401 | credential/API-key problem |\n| 403 | IAM / bearer-token permission / model authorization |\n| 404 | wrong URL/API route/model identifier |\n| validation error | request payload/API mismatch |\n| model unavailable | regional/model-access issue |\n| 429 | quota/throttling |\n| `BEDROCK_OK` | AWS path works; GCE/OpenCode integration is the problem |\n\nThere is one credential wrinkle worth flagging. Current AWS documentation distinguishes the permission to **use an API key against Mantle** as `bedrock-mantle:CallWithBearerToken`, while actual inference authorization is associated with the Mantle inference permissions. So generating a fresh-looking credential does **not automatically prove that the principal can use it against that endpoint**. citeturn383755search2\n\nAnd I think this explains why this has felt absurdly complicated: we may have been debugging **four variables simultaneously**:\n\n**credential → endpoint → region → model/API**\n\ninstead of freezing three and testing one.\n\n### What I want us to do now\n\nKeep Luce doing the full Truth Tower.\n\nFor our working lane, I would freeze **`us-east-2 + Mantle + Kimi K2.5` as the control case**. If that single call works, we immediately know the $140 runway is usable and can work outward from there into GLM/DeepSeek/OpenCode. If it doesn't work, give me the **exact sanitized error response** from that one call—not the whole history—and we can usually classify it in one pass.\n\nAWS itself confirms that `us-east-2` supports the Mantle endpoint, and Kimi K2.5, DeepSeek V3.2, and several other models are actually available there. So your instinct that this is probably a **configuration/region/invocation-path issue rather than “Bedrock simply doesn't work”** is technically plausible. citeturn383755search0turn383755search1 memcite", "text_chars": 4169, "code_blocks": 3, "links": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1", "https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`", "https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/openai/v1`"], "citations": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1", "https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`", "https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/openai/v1`"], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1e3fb00e-bfbe-4cb0-9a3d-af2ec77d21c6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214436.802163, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c37c0df4-a14e-4bff-9908-d818d664d3a6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790214436.806893, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "58cc2c38-8527-4b4e-b6df-db9e0dc4d762", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215405.165, "updated_at": 1790215423.584912, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "All right, give Don what— okay, so All right. Where are we at? Don is fucking hungry. That's where we're at. All right, give Don, give Don what I need to look at side by side. I'm looking at it. ", "text_chars": 195, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "72a9c830-8c0b-4152-8bee-66088a348f11", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215408.351967, "updated_at": 1790215423.419798, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "You’re **in the right AWS account**, and the screenshot gives us two very useful facts immediately:\n\n- **Credits remaining: $159.26**\n- **Current month spend: $0.74**\n- Your console is currently set to **United States (N. Virginia)** — that is **`us-east-1`**\n- Our control-path target has been **Ohio / `us-east-2`**\n\nSo the **first thing I want you to check side by side is region**. That mismatch could absolutely explain part of the chaos.\n\n### Put these side by side\n\n| What Don sees | What we want for the control test |\n|---|---|\n| AWS account `280768229421` | Same account |\n| Console region: **N. Virginia** | **Ohio (`us-east-2`)** |\n| Credits: **$159.26** | Good — runway confirmed |\n| Bedrock console | Bedrock in **us-east-2** |\n| Mantle/API config | `bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws` |\n| Model | `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5` |\n\n### Do this now\n\nClick the region selector in the **top right** where it says:\n\n**United States (N. Virginia)**\n\nChange it to:\n\n**US East (Ohio)**\n\nThat should put the console into:\n\n```text\nus-east-2\n```\n\nThen click **Amazon Bedrock (mantle endpoint...)** from your Recently visited list.\n\nOnce you’re inside, don’t change anything yet. Send me the next screenshot.\n\nWe are going to walk this in this order:\n\n**Account → Region → Bedrock/Mantle → model visibility → credential → tiny API test**\n\nAnd your screenshot already resolves one big question: **you have $159.26 of AWS credits sitting there. We are not broke on AWS.** The immediate suspect is now configuration/routing, not funding. memcite", "text_chars": 1539, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "bda902c4-fdb3-413a-94e2-09d980598ab9", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215408.3525813, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "53a0e7db-2225-40fa-b835-d00e7593901c", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215413.019272, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "378882ba-c523-42e1-b299-5ae73002a03b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215491.14, "updated_at": 1790215528.951898, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "Please document the shit out of this because I think it's just a mix-up between models and region. NIDs. So whoever we're going to give this to in terminal needs to have everything documented to test, or I could do it in PowerShell. I'm coherent. I am knowledgeable enough to do— if you give Don the PowerShell commands. My guess is you want Don to go to API keys. ", "text_chars": 365, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "bb0193ea-7fca-40f1-aa96-62968a121453", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215494.401564, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "44e925fa-c203-4c9e-8561-e4ba81f83bdc", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790215496.1351671, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "179bfac3-3cc0-4032-ba42-39840a8a21c5", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790215496.1394212, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8364d9ae-7fab-4525-a26a-495c60bacace", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215496.732035, "updated_at": 1790215528.524452, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — **API Keys is the right next place to look**, but don’t create or rotate anything yet.\n\nAnd I want to document one correction immediately because this may be the exact source of the mess:\n\n> **AWS’s current generic API-key support page does not list `us-east-2` (Ohio) among the regions supporting Bedrock API keys**, even though Kimi K2.5 and DeepSeek V3.2 themselves *are* available for in-region inference in `us-east-2`. citeturn179152search10turn179152search1turn179152search3\n\nThat means we may have been conflating **model region support** with **API-key support**. Those are separate dimensions.\n\n## What the screenshot proves\n\nYou are now in:\n\n```text\nAWS account: 280768229421\nConsole: Amazon Bedrock — bedrock-mantle endpoint\nRegion: US East (Ohio)\nRegion ID: us-east-2\nProject scope: default\n```\n\nThe console itself is also explicitly presenting:\n\n- **Models**\n- **Workbench**\n- **API keys**\n- **Live API docs**\n- both the **bedrock-mantle** and **bedrock-runtime** concepts\n\nSo we are absolutely looking at the right AWS service surface.\n\nAWS currently documents Kimi K2.5 as supporting both `bedrock-runtime` and `bedrock-mantle`, with model ID:\n\n```text\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n```\n\nand it supports in-region inference in both `us-east-1` and `us-east-2`. citeturn179152search1turn179152search3\n\n---\n\n# Don: click **API keys**\n\nLeft side, under **ACCOUNT SCOPE → API keys**.\n\n### Do not create one yet.\n\nI want to see:\n\n- what keys already exist;\n- short-term vs long-term;\n- their state;\n- creation/expiration;\n- whether AWS associates them with a particular region or scope;\n- whether the console gives you any warning in Ohio.\n\n**Do not show me an actual key value.** Key names, IDs, dates, status, and metadata are fine.\n\nSend me that screenshot.\n\n---\n\n# Meanwhile: here is our documented test matrix\n\nThis is what either you or the terminal agent should execute. We will change **one variable at a time**.\n\n| Test | Region | Endpoint | Model | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | `us-east-2` | Mantle | Kimi K2.5 | Current suspected path |\n| B | `us-east-1` | Mantle | Kimi K2.5 | Isolate API-key/region issue |\n| C | `us-east-2` | Runtime | Kimi K2.5 | Isolate Mantle from model |\n| D | `us-east-1` | Runtime | Kimi K2.5 | Known broadly supported control |\n| E | working region | Mantle | DeepSeek V3.2 | Cross-model verification |\n\n**Nothing else changes during each test.**\n\n---\n\n# PowerShell kit — safe diagnostics first\n\nYou can run these yourself.\n\n### 1. AWS CLI identity\n\n```powershell\naws sts get-caller-identity\n```\n\nExpected shape:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"UserId\": \"...\",\n    \"Account\": \"280768229421\",\n    \"Arn\": \"arn:aws:iam::280768229421:user/...\"\n}\n```\n\nNo secret is exposed by this command.\n\n### 2. See what region your CLI thinks it is using\n\n```powershell\naws configure get region\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\n$env:AWS_REGION\n$env:AWS_DEFAULT_REGION\n```\n\nIf those disagree, **document it**. Do not fix it yet.\n\n### 3. Inspect relevant environment variables without printing secrets\n\nUse this instead of echoing the key:\n\n```powershell\nif ($env:OPENAI_API_KEY) {\n    \"OPENAI_API_KEY = PRESENT, length $($env:OPENAI_API_KEY.Length)\"\n} else {\n    \"OPENAI_API_KEY = ABSENT\"\n}\n\nif ($env:AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK) {\n    \"AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK = PRESENT, length $($env:AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK.Length)\"\n} else {\n    \"AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK = ABSENT\"\n}\n\n\"OPENAI_BASE_URL = $env:OPENAI_BASE_URL\"\n\"AWS_REGION = $env:AWS_REGION\"\n\"AWS_DEFAULT_REGION = $env:AWS_DEFAULT_REGION\"\n```\n\nThis could be extremely revealing.\n\nIf, for example, we find:\n\n```text\nOPENAI_BASE_URL = ...us-east-1...\nAWS_REGION = us-east-2\n```\n\nor vice versa, we have a configuration collision.\n\n---\n\n# One thing I do **not** want yet\n\nDo **not** globally set this:\n\n```powershell\n$env:OPENAI_API_KEY = \"...\"\n```\n\nuntil we know which credential we're testing.\n\nAnd definitely don't paste the key into chat.\n\nOnce we establish the active key, we'll put it into the current PowerShell process only, run one microscopic request, and close the shell afterward if desired.\n\n---\n\n# Critical endpoint distinction\n\nAWS currently documents these as separate OpenAI-compatible surfaces:\n\n### Bedrock runtime\n\n```text\nhttps://bedrock-runtime.<region>.amazonaws.com/openai/v1\n```\n\n### Bedrock Mantle\n\n```text\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.<region>.api.aws/v1\n```\n\nAWS explicitly says that when using the OpenAI SDK, the Bedrock API key goes in `OPENAI_API_KEY`, and the corresponding Bedrock URL goes in `OPENAI_BASE_URL`. citeturn179152search5\n\nFor Kimi specifically, AWS's model card gives the model ID as:\n\n```text\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n```\n\nnot `kimi-k2.5`, not a deployment name, and not an ARN. citeturn179152search1\n\nThat's another place I want us to be ruthless about exact IDs.\n\n---\n\n## Working hypothesis\n\nI now think there are **three especially plausible mix-ups**:\n\n1. **Ohio model availability ≠ Ohio API-key availability.**\n2. We may have mixed **Mantle URLs and runtime URLs** between tests.\n3. We may have used a legitimate model in a legitimate region with a credential mechanism that isn't supported in that exact combination.\n\nThat would perfectly explain the frustrating pattern of:\n\n> “Everything looks configured. Why the hell won't it connect?”\n\nAnd the good news is that this is **testable without redesigning anything**.\n\n**Next move: click `API keys` and send me that screen.** Then I'll tell you exactly what to inspect before we touch a credential.", "text_chars": 5467, "code_blocks": 12, "links": ["https://bedrock-mantle.", "https://bedrock-runtime."], "citations": ["https://bedrock-mantle.", "https://bedrock-runtime."], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "29096117-d91d-4784-8341-5d3554dda547", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215499.897034, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0570320c-f3fd-47a6-b1e4-2bf9d865ff13", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215499.90243, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a4d2efc5-7c00-417d-b277-4a17ce3874e4", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790215528.579, "updated_at": 1790215570.163311, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": fals