a-messages.json: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'C:\\\\Users\\\\DEKANA~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\nova-messages.json'\r\nPS C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother>\n\naws: [ERROR]: An error occurred (ValidationException) when calling the Converse operation: Operation not allowed\r\nPS C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother>\n\n\nOkay, so I tried both your things. Okay. I'm gonna chime in here. Could this be a region issue? ", "text_chars": 4093, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\nova-messages.json", "1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\nova-messages.json", "C:\\Users\\Dekan", "C:\\\\Users\\\\DEKANA~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\nova-messages.json"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d209cf75-a54e-4260-9599-addca2c99a98", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216295.114819, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "bio", "content_type": "code", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f7a2625f-26ab-46fe-9fd2-60e569eefab4", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216296.271376, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4f7a0e87-fc6e-43e1-b510-5aecbb43a0a7", "role": "tool", "role_name": "bio", "created_at": 1790216307.545627, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "assistant", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Model set context updated.", "text_chars": 26, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a7c4537f-5c2b-4bc4-a157-1ee1008dc478", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216310.009438, "updated_at": 1790216330.597079, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — **region/routing is now the leading explanation for the Nova 2 Lite failure**, but with one precise twist:\n\nAWS currently shows **Nova 2 Lite is *not* available for single-region inference in `us-east-2`**. Ohio supports it through **US Geo** or **Global cross-region inference** instead. citeturn470143search1turn470143search0\n\nThat reconciles the apparently contradictory facts we just observed:\n\n- `amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0` appears as **ACTIVE** in the Bedrock model catalog.\n- Direct `Converse` against the raw ID in `us-east-2` returns **`ValidationException: Operation not allowed`**.\n- AWS says the US cross-region ID from Ohio is:\n\n```text\nus.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\nand Ohio is a supported **source region** for that US Geo inference profile. citeturn470143search0\n\nThere are actually **two separate failures** in your last test sequence:\n\n```text\nNo such file or directory: nova-messages.json\n```\n\nThat one is purely local — the temp file didn't exist.\n\nThen:\n\n```text\nValidationException: Operation not allowed\n```\n\nThat one is AWS/runtime routing.\n\n## Let's remove every other variable\n\nDon't use the temp files. Don't use raw `amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0`.\n\nRun **one** command with the US inference profile, but use PowerShell's stop-parsing operator so it doesn't destroy the JSON:\n\n```powershell\naws --% bedrock-runtime converse --region us-east-2 --model-id us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0 --messages \"[{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Return exactly: NOVA_OK\\\"}]}]\" --inference-config \"{\\\"maxTokens\\\":20,\\\"temperature\\\":0}\"\n```\n\nIf that still gives us grief over Windows quoting, I want to switch to a tiny PowerShell-generated JSON file in the **current directory**, not `%TEMP%`, so we can visibly confirm it exists before invoking.\n\n### One more useful discovery\n\nThe older **Nova Lite** is different. AWS shows `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` has **direct in-region support in Ohio**, whereas Nova **2** Lite does not. citeturn470143search2\n\nSo we now have an excellent A/B control:\n\n```text\nNova Lite:\namazon.nova-lite-v1:0\nOhio direct inference supported\n\nNova 2 Lite:\namazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\nOhio direct inference NOT supported\nUS Geo ID required:\nus.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\nIf needed, we can test old Nova Lite directly and Nova 2 Lite via the `us.` profile. That will prove the routing distinction beyond doubt.\n\nAnd yes — **I saved the full Mantle inventory you just extracted**, including Kimi 2.5, Kimi Thinking, GLM 5, DeepSeek V3.2, Grok 4.3, the OpenAI 5.x models, Qwen, Mistral, Nemotron, MiniMax, Gemma, and Claude Haiku 4.5, along with the fact that Kimi 2.5 has already passed live inference. memcite\n\nAfter we crack Nova, I absolutely want to do the **super-extraction by price**. That model list is much richer than I expected, and with $159.26 sitting there we can build a very serious GCE routing map.", "text_chars": 2864, "code_blocks": 5, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["nova-messages.json"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "352ec7d6-0390-4e85-a7f9-18ca1ee23767", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216354.041, "updated_at": 1790216382.614845, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay. So I got the same stupid error about when calling ConverseOperation, validation exception. ", "text_chars": 97, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0f4e65b4-1eb6-4b15-9b1b-1adcb6783032", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216357.163391, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "2544e944-29c0-4ff5-bf85-a2b3cedd272d", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216359.3462026, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "021da07c-4901-4466-8ffb-ac773da82c45", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216359.3509924, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "da4189c5-996f-4a4f-acb7-76c6afe7417c", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216359.961739, "updated_at": 1790216382.938717, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "**Yes. At this point I would explicitly test region.** The fact that `us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0` still returns **`ValidationException: Operation not allowed`** from Ohio is valuable: AWS documentation says that US inference profile *should* be callable from `us-east-2`, so either cross-region routing is blocked for this principal/account or we have a Nova-specific account restriction. citeturn802587search0turn802587search9\n\nAWS separately publishes a direct Nova 2 Lite example using **N. Virginia (`us-east-1`)** with the raw model ID `amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0`. citeturn802587search5\n\nSo let's do the cleanest A/B test possible.\n\n### Next step — **only test N. Virginia**\n\nFirst, don't change your AWS default region globally. Just issue this control-plane check:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock get-inference-profile `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --inference-profile-identifier us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\n**Stop after that and paste the result.**\n\nThis costs nothing and tells us whether your `PeteW` principal can even resolve the US Nova inference profile from Ohio.\n\nThere are only two meaningful branches:\n\n- **It returns profile details:** Ohio can see the CRIS route, and we investigate invocation/IAM next.\n- **It errors:** we've isolated the failure to **cross-region profile access/routing**, which makes the N. Virginia direct-model test the obvious next control.\n\nAnd importantly, we are **not touching the working Kimi/Mantle configuration**. That path is now sacred until this Nova issue is understood. memcite", "text_chars": 1536, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "edf06fbe-44fe-4a71-8af4-7a9668c889a0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216368.375183, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1d0bcbc1-ae94-4cc0-81c5-533ba30841c6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216372.338489, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6e05ee36-b84b-446e-aefa-0c09efae5093", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216372.341736, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3fa8db2a-05c0-415d-9bf1-d990474ebf4b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216408.322, "updated_at": 1790216433.857762, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Oh, someone knows what he's doing. See, in Azure I was able to use multiple regions and multiple deployments per region.   PS C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother> aws bedrock get-inference-profile `\r\n>>   --region us-east-2 `\r\n>>   --inference-profile-identifier us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\r\n{\r\n    \"inferenceProfileName\": \"US Amazon Nova 2 Lite\",\r\n    \"description\": \"Routes requests to Amazon Nova 2 Lite in us-west-2, us-east-1 and us-east-2.\",\r\n    \"createdAt\": \"2025-10-30T21:27:02.585000+00:00\",\r\n    \"updatedAt\": \"2026-03-24T17:43:50.968000+00:00\",\r\n    \"inferenceProfileArn\": \"arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-2:280768229421:inference-profile/us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\",\r\n    \"models\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"modelArn\": \"arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"modelArn\": \"arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"modelArn\": \"arn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\"\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"inferenceProfileId\": \"us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\",\r\n    \"status\": \"ACTIVE\",\r\n    \"type\": \"SYSTEM_DEFINED\"", "text_chars": 1149, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["C:\\Users\\Dekan"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "41261ea8-8e45-429a-9ae8-46d0a6a54dfa", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216411.619294, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "ef2afe42-f9f7-4124-9708-e773fd035c7b", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216418.0646656, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "50912db7-7444-44e0-b4ea-e1d74dbedac7", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216418.0694573, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "f8a38237-188f-4c20-9fd2-a5acdd8ed1ca", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216418.658573, "updated_at": 1790216457.222267, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Exactly. **That result kills the “wrong region/profile doesn’t exist” hypothesis.**\n\nYour account in `us-east-2` can resolve an **ACTIVE US cross-region inference profile** for Nova 2 Lite, and AWS is explicitly telling us the profile can route to:\n\n- `us-east-1`\n- `us-east-2`\n- `us-west-2`\n\nSo the remaining suspect is now **authorization across the inference profile and all destination-region foundation-model ARNs**, not basic region discovery. AWS requires `bedrock:InvokeModel` permission on the inference profile **and** on the foundation model in the source and every destination region in the profile. A deny/SCP on even one destination can break cross-region inference. citeturn108679search0turn108679search1\n\nThis is very Azure-like conceptually: **one logical deployment/profile, multiple regional backends**, except AWS makes the IAM evaluation across those routing targets more explicit.\n\n## Next step: inspect Don’s actual Bedrock permissions\n\nRun this:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-attached-user-policies `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --output table\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-user-policies `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --output table\n```\n\nDo **not** change IAM yet. I just want to see whether `PeteW` has something broad like:\n\n```text\nAmazonBedrockFullAccess\n```\n\nor whether we're dealing with custom inline policies.\n\nIf `AmazonBedrockFullAccess` is already attached, then we pivot immediately to **SCP / explicit deny / model access**.\n\nIf it is **not** attached, the likely defect is that the current policy allows Mantle but does not grant the classic Bedrock runtime action:\n\n```text\nbedrock:InvokeModel\n```\n\nacross:\n\n```text\narn:aws:bedrock:us-east-2:280768229421:inference-profile/us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\narn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\narn:aws:bedrock:us-east-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\narn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\nAWS documents that exact permission pattern for geographic cross-region inference. citeturn108679search0turn108679search6\n\nSo our troubleshooting tree is now beautifully narrow:\n\n**Mantle/Kimi works ✅**  \n**Nova profile exists ✅**  \n**Nova profile ACTIVE ✅**  \n**Profile routes across three US regions ✅**  \n**Converse still blocked ❌**  \n→ **IAM/SCP authorization is now the primary suspect.**\n\nRun those two IAM listing commands. That should tell us very quickly which branch we're on.", "text_chars": 2442, "code_blocks": 5, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "40a5863c-120c-48de-9365-bf615d5f0c27", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216419.668564, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0d3f6de6-a582-4dae-b0c2-fdc9671341d5", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216419.675124, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e67ef35f-6284-43aa-b1cc-75a2f3975d1a", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216467.319, "updated_at": 1790216481.998508, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": ">   --user-name PeteW `\r\n>>   --output table\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n|                     ListAttachedUserPolicies                     |\r\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\r\n||                        AttachedPolicies                        ||\r\n|+-------------------------------------------+--------------------+|\r\n||                 PolicyArn                 |    PolicyName      ||\r\n|+-------------------------------------------+--------------------+|\r\n||  arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSSupportAccess |  AWSSupportAccess  ||\r\n|+-------------------------------------------+--------------------+|\r\n", "text_chars": 676, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "acc6a122-5942-4e7e-ac0c-a7a4334c9f60", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216470.455963, "updated_at": 1790216481.99887, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "**That is a huge clue.** Right now, for **directly attached managed policies**, `PeteW` only has:\n\n```text\nAWSSupportAccess\n```\n\nSo there is **no directly attached Bedrock managed policy** on the user.\n\nThat fits the pattern we’re seeing:\n\n- **Mantle + API key + Kimi works**\n- **Classic `bedrock-runtime Converse` fails with `Operation not allowed`**\n\nBut we are **not allowed to conclude IAM is missing yet**, because `PeteW` could still be getting Bedrock permissions from:\n1. an **inline user policy**, or\n2. an **IAM group**.\n\n### Next command only\n\nRun:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-user-policies `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --output table\n```\n\nPaste that output.\n\nThen we’ll check groups.\n\nDo **not** attach `AmazonBedrockFullAccess` yet. We’re going to prove exactly where your current permissions come from before changing anything.", "text_chars": 838, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "88f5e831-a086-4e80-9cf3-f2648e3daaf5", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216474.729556, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5e39765b-f5ac-4901-8f37-85bbd5a02bcc", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216501.97, "updated_at": 1790216511.92958, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "|     ListUserPolicies     |\r\n+--------------------------+\r\n||       PolicyNames      ||\r\n|+------------------------+|\r\n||  SupportConsoleAccess  ||\r\n|+------------------------+|", "text_chars": 178, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2be0eb19-22b8-468e-bfb8-8938cd105920", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216505.175575, "updated_at": 1790216516.928663, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Good. That narrows it further.\n\nSo far, `PeteW` has:\n\n- Managed user policy: `AWSSupportAccess`\n- Inline user policy: `SupportConsoleAccess`\n\nNeither name suggests Bedrock runtime authority.\n\nBut we still need to check **group-based permissions** before concluding anything.\n\nRun this next:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-groups-for-user `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --output table\n```\n\nPaste the output.\n\nIf there are groups, we’ll inspect their attached and inline policies next. If there are **no groups**, then we’ll inspect the actual JSON inside `SupportConsoleAccess` and we’ll likely have isolated why classic `bedrock-runtime Converse` is blocked while Mantle API-key inference works.", "text_chars": 687, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a857a612-2c6c-4750-a4b3-1d776006c2de", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216507.032285, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ba11c8a1-0488-4478-ac91-2e9519c1f1ec", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216535.487, "updated_at": 1790216546.298593, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I'm not changing anything. I thought I set this up pretty good.   ---------------------------------------------------------\r\n|                   ListGroupsForUser                   |\r\n+-------------------------------------------------------+\r\n||                       Groups                        ||\r\n|+-------------+---------------------------------------+|\r\n||  Arn        |  arn:aws:iam::280768229421:group/GCE  ||\r\n||  CreateDate |  2026-07-08T06:06:42+00:00            ||\r\n||  GroupId    |  AGPAUCXYXGAW7OT3MYVDT                ||\r\n||  GroupName  |  GCE                                  ||\r\n||  Path       |  /                                    ||\r\n|+-------------+---------------------------------------+|\r\n\r\nPS C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother>", "text_chars": 752, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["C:\\Users\\Dekan"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4e75b579-77c9-4f2a-9bd5-c92e84062b3a", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216538.652913, "updated_at": 1790216573.196643, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "That actually looks **more promising**, not worse.\n\n`PeteW` is in the **GCE** IAM group, so the Bedrock permissions may be attached there rather than directly to the user. That would be a sensible setup.\n\n### Next command only\n\nRun:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-attached-group-policies `\n  --group-name GCE `\n  --output table\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-group-policies `\n  --group-name GCE `\n  --output table\n```\n\nWe are looking for either:\n\n- an AWS-managed Bedrock policy,\n- a custom GCE Bedrock policy,\n- or an inline policy granting `bedrock:*`, `bedrock:InvokeModel`, inference-profile access, or Mantle permissions.\n\n**Do not change anything.** Paste both outputs and we’ll keep tracing the actual permission path.", "text_chars": 734, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cef10792-ee85-451e-abd1-c8ad2c821fa5", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216572.57, "updated_at": 1790216597.51137, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "PS C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother> aws iam list-attached-group-policies `\r\n>>   --group-name GCE `\r\n>>   --output table\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n|                        ListAttachedGroupPolicies                       |\r\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------+\r\n||                           AttachedPolicies                           ||\r\n|+----------------------------------------------+-----------------------+|\r\n||                   PolicyArn                  |      PolicyName       ||\r\n|+----------------------------------------------+-----------------------+|\r\n||  arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AdministratorAccess |  AdministratorAccess  ||\r\n|+----------------------------------------------+-----------------------+|\r\n", "text_chars": 800, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["C:\\Users\\Dekan"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8d4437f3-c24f-4078-9fb3-22c50da45aa0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216575.739786, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8f2247d8-a02a-4113-aaa0-b5ec634a7ff9", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216580.9666636, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "6fe6427d-d856-489f-84b9-27dded0c376c", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216580.9725213, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "4fe7e72c-9582-421f-afd9-f26e1eddc946", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216581.539022, "updated_at": 1790216599.133581, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "That changes the diagnosis **materially**.\n\n`PeteW` inherits **AdministratorAccess** through the `GCE` group. So absent a permissions boundary, SCP, or some service-side account restriction, ordinary IAM permissions are **not** the problem.\n\nAnd I found something very relevant: AWS re:Post has current reports of this **exact** pattern — `ValidationException: Operation not allowed` on Bedrock `Converse`, even when IAM is correct, the model is active, billing is valid, and the inference profile exists. In those cases the issue was an **account/service-level Bedrock runtime restriction/allowlisting condition**, not malformed JSON or missing `bedrock:InvokeModel`. citeturn362763search0turn362763search2\n\nSo our state is now:\n\n```text\nPeteW IAM user                     ✅\nGCE group membership               ✅\nAdministratorAccess via GCE        ✅\nBedrock control-plane access       ✅\nNova 2 Lite profile ACTIVE         ✅\nUS CRIS profile resolves           ✅\nMantle inference (Kimi 2.5)        ✅\nClassic Runtime Converse           ❌ \"Operation not allowed\"\n```\n\nThat is a **very distinctive split**.\n\n## One more IAM sanity check\n\nBefore I call this account/runtime-side, I want to rule out a permissions boundary on `PeteW`.\n\nRun only:\n\n```powershell\naws iam get-user `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --query \"User.PermissionsBoundary\" `\n  --output json\n```\n\nIf it returns:\n\n```text\nnull\n```\n\nthen there is no user permissions boundary constraining that AdministratorAccess.\n\nAfter that, the remaining high-value checks are **not more credential rotations** and **not more IAM policy changes**. We would inspect:\n\n1. whether the AWS account belongs to an Organization/SCP,\n2. Bedrock Runtime quotas/allowlisting state,\n3. direct Nova Lite vs Nova 2 Lite behavior,\n4. and, if necessary, the AWS Support/account-activation path.\n\nAWS re:Post specifically documents cases where token-generating Bedrock Runtime operations sit at account quotas of `0` and return this exact `Operation not allowed` error even though listing models/profiles works. citeturn362763search2\n\nSo you did, in fact, set IAM up pretty well. **AdministratorAccess through the GCE group is a coherent design.** The evidence is moving away from “Don misconfigured permissions” and toward **“Bedrock Runtime is gated on the account while Mantle is not.”**", "text_chars": 2324, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8213417a-57e5-49bc-9df9-2b871a7f45e5", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216582.590652, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f5145001-dee4-4b83-b5c0-90a5690bf6de", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216582.596931, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1ce3213a-0997-4407-b9a2-59867bee7f31", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216618.209, "updated_at": 1790216647.896254, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "PS C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother> aws iam list-group-policies `\r\n>>   --group-name GCE `\r\n>>   --output table\r\n-------------------\r\n|ListGroupPolicies|\n\n\nYeah, return null. ", "text_chars": 169, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["C:\\Users\\Dekan"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "aa81968d-f2a3-470a-9a9f-e908fab0dbdd", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216621.507646, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "a488bf40-23a8-4a5b-95c1-d5917dcc4641", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216623.6689312, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "e30c4c30-3d35-4778-acd8-e1e18af21567", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790216623.676757, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "af0c213c-3c0f-4008-b5d3-6a5dd656998f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216624.541333, "updated_at": 1790216690.520909, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Perfect. **That closes the IAM branch.**\n\nCurrent permission picture:\n\n- `PeteW` direct managed policy: `AWSSupportAccess`\n- `PeteW` inline policy: `SupportConsoleAccess`\n- `PeteW` group: `GCE`\n- `GCE` attached managed policy: **`AdministratorAccess`**\n- `GCE` inline policies: **none**\n- `PeteW` permissions boundary: **null**\n\nSo there is no obvious IAM-side reason why `bedrock:InvokeModel` should be denied. AWS documents `InvokeModel` as the permission underlying both direct model invocation and Converse-family access. citeturn338046search3turn338046search6\n\nAt this point, I would **stop changing credentials or IAM entirely**.\n\nThe strongest remaining hypothesis is **Bedrock Runtime quota/account provisioning**, because AWS says `bedrock-runtime` inference is governed by separate per-model quotas, while **Mantle traffic is counted separately**. That fits our exact split: Kimi works through Mantle, while Nova Runtime returns `ValidationException: Operation not allowed`. citeturn338046search1\n\nThere are recent AWS re:Post cases with the same symptom pattern: model listing succeeds, IAM is correct, but Nova Converse returns `Operation not allowed`; in at least one case the account showed **RPM/TPM = 0 for Nova**. That isn't proof your account has the same condition, but it is now the right thing to test. citeturn338046search0turn338046search2\n\n### Next command only\n\nLet's inspect the actual Bedrock service quotas available to your account in Ohio:\n\n```powershell\naws service-quotas list-service-quotas `\n  --service-code bedrock `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --query \"Quotas[?contains(QuotaName, 'Nova')].[QuotaName,Value,Adjustable]\" `\n  --output table\n```\n\nIf that throws another table-format annoyance, use:\n\n```powershell\naws service-quotas list-service-quotas `\n  --service-code bedrock `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --query \"Quotas[?contains(QuotaName, 'Nova')]\" `\n  --output json\n```\n\nWhat I care about is whether Nova shows **`0` RPM / `0` TPM** or some other restricted value.\n\nIf it does, we’ve probably found the real root cause:\n\n> **Mantle provisioned/usable; classic Bedrock Runtime token-generating quota not provisioned for Nova on this account.**\n\nThat would also explain why the Playground itself gave you grief even though the model catalog and inference profile looked perfectly healthy.", "text_chars": 2334, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e3cd1a1d-8457-4924-b2c1-2a9259cba75b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216629.029209, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e6fb9ee6-ee18-46a0-a8fe-285fb51714e8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790216629.049637, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": 