tokens per minute for Amazon Nova 2 Lite   0.0\n```\n\nAnd it’s broader than Nova 2 Lite. Nova Pro, Micro, Premier, Omni, etc. are all showing the same pattern: **token-generating runtime quotas at 0.0**.\n\nSo the `ValidationException: Operation not allowed` now makes sense.\n\n### What is actually working\n\nYour **Mantle path is healthy**:\n\n```text\nus-east-2\n→ bedrock-mantle\n→ API key auth\n→ /models\n→ moonshotai.kimi-k2.5 available\n→ live inference succeeds\n```\n\nYour **classic Bedrock Runtime path is account-gated by zero quotas** for Nova:\n\n```text\nus-east-2\n→ bedrock-runtime / Converse\n→ Nova profile resolves\n→ IAM is effectively admin\n→ runtime quota = 0\n→ Operation not allowed\n```\n\nThat is the clean explanation.\n\n### Important nuance\n\nSome of those quota rows say `Adjustable = True`, especially TPM-style quotas, while others are non-adjustable. That means there may be a request path through **Service Quotas** for some dimensions, but this is no longer an IAM or credentials problem.\n\nAt this point I would stop spending any more time trying different Nova model IDs or regions until the runtime quota gate is addressed.\n\n### Operational conclusion\n\nFor GCE **right now**:\n\n- **Kimi 2.5 via Mantle: usable**\n- **Kimi K2 Thinking via Mantle: visible**\n- **DeepSeek / GLM / Qwen / Grok / OpenAI / Mistral / Nemotron / MiniMax / Gemma / Haiku via Mantle: visible**\n- **Nova via classic Runtime: blocked by zero account quota**\n- **AWS credits: still usable through Mantle**\n\nThat is actually good news, because Mantle gives you a large model estate even while Nova Runtime is gated.\n\nThe next high-value move is the **super extraction by cost and capability** across your live Mantle inventory, then we can decide which models become default, cheap-worker, coder, verifier, and escalation lanes while the Nova quota issue is handled separately. memcite", "text_chars": 2351, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references