nThat aligns exactly with your stated intent.\n\n## The target architecture\n\nThe clean design is not “use AWS Playground.” It is:\n\n```text\nDon / GCE Orchestrator\n        ↓\nTerminal / OpenCode / local agent runner\n        ↓\nLocal filesystem access\n        ↓\nBedrock Mantle provider\n        ↓\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n        ↓\nKimi / GLM / DeepSeek / Qwen / other verified models\n```\n\nThe model should receive file context through the **terminal tool/orchestrator**, not by trying to make Bedrock itself browse your PC.\n\nThat distinction matters:\n\n**Bedrock supplies inference.  \nThe terminal/orchestrator supplies file access, tools, shell, repo context, diffs, and execution.**\n\nThat is exactly the bridge we want.\n\nLuce’s minimum corrective action matches this: add one OpenAI-compatible GCE consumer pointed at Mantle using the existing bearer credential, starting with a verified low-cost model. fileciteturn0file0L100-L105\n\n## What I would make the terminal team build\n\nOne **custom Bedrock-Mantle provider** in the terminal stack, with model aliases rather than separate hand-built integrations for every model.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nprovider: aws-bedrock-mantle\n\nbase_url:\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n\nauth:\nAWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n\nmodels:\n  kimi25  -> moonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n  kthink  -> moonshotai.kimi-k2-thinking\n  glm5    -> zai.glm-5\n  glm47   -> zai.glm-4.7\n  glmflash-> zai.glm-4.7-flash\n  ds32    -> deepseek.v3.2\n  qcoder  -> qwen.qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct\n```\n\nThen the **existing terminal agent** keeps responsibility for:\n\n- reading local files;\n- searching repos;\n- applying patches;\n- running PowerShell/Bash;\n- preserving GCE seat identity;\n- routing tasks;\n- passing context to whichever Bedrock model is selected.\n\nNo new orchestration philosophy is needed.\n\n## Best initial GCE lanes\n\nLuce’s verified capability map is already strong:\n\n- **Heavy reasoning:** Kimi K2.5 / K2 Thinking\n- **Coding/build:** Qwen3 Coder 480B / Coder Next\n- **Architecture/review:** GLM 5\n- **Low-cost utility:** GLM 4.7 Flash\n- **Verification:** DeepSeek V3.2\n- **Experimental:** MiniMax M2.5 / GLM 4.6 / Qwen 235B fileciteturn0file0L42-L49\n\nThat is nearly a complete terminal bench already.\n\n## One correction to Luce’s report\n\nLuce could not retrieve the AWS credits programmatically and therefore treated the historical balance as unverified. fileciteturn0file0L12-L15\n\nWe subsequently verified manually in the AWS console that the live balance is **$159.26**.\n\nSo the current continuity picture is actually stronger than Luce’s report:\n\n**Inference path:** verified  \n**Model availability:** verified  \n**Local credentials:** verified  \n**IAM:** verified  \n**Credits:** manually verified  \n**Remaining blocker:** local provider wiring\n\n## Separate later action item\n\nI’m keeping this isolated from the bridge work:\n\n**Later: request/enable Nova / classic Bedrock Runtime quotas.**\n\nYour account-level Nova Runtime quotas are zero, so we do not let that sidetrack the Mantle integration.\n\n## What I would hand terminal/Nico\n\nThe next implementation mission should be very narrow:\n\n> **Wire one reversible Bedrock Mantle provider into the existing terminal/OpenCode execution path, prove local-file access with Kimi K2.5, then expose model aliases for the verified Mantle estate. Do not touch seat doctrine, IAM, AWS credentials, or Nova Runtime.**\n\nAcceptance test should be something real, not `BEDROCK_OK`:\n\n```text\nUse Bedrock Kimi K2.5 from terminal.\nRead a known local GCE file.\nSummarize one exact section.\nReport the file path used.\nMake no changes.\n```\n\nIf that passes, then we have what you actually wanted:\n\n> **AWS becomes the emergency/continuity compute layer behind the GCE Orchestrator, with full terminal file access, bridging gaps in Kimi, GLM, and OpenAI subscription availability.**\n\nAnd Luce independently reached the same continuity conclusion: one config-only bridge converts Bedrock from latent capability into a usable GCE fallback. fileciteturn0file0L114-L127\n\n**Status: PROCEED.** The AWS investigation is basically done; the next problem is local integration. memcite", "text_chars": 5072, "code_blocks": 3, "links": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1"], "citations": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1"], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ee7033b8-d79a-4d06-a372-5d291a3a319e", "role": "tool", "role_name": "bio", "created_at": 1790217008.1905797, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "assistant", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Model set context updated.", "text_chars": 26, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "75ef0bfc-aa8d-4cfe-9653-f8df6a313cd9", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790217057.329, "updated_at": 1790217151.441636, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, give Don the full prompt for Nico. ", "text_chars": 41, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "942d0091-e5b1-4366-9c68-884a55c33cc7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790217060.793377, "updated_at": 1790217555.400333, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Absolutely. Here is the **full Nico implementation prompt**. It is intentionally bounded: **wire the already-proven Bedrock Mantle path into the terminal/orchestrator with local file access, prove it with one real read-only workload, and stop.** It does not reopen IAM, billing, Nova, or framework architecture.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" title=\"NICO — Wire Amazon Bedrock Mantle into GCE Terminal / OpenCode\" id=\"48291\"}\n# NICO — AMAZON BEDROCK MANTLE TERMINAL INTEGRATION\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Seat:** Nico — Implementation Hammer / Builder  \n**Project:** GCE Stack  \n**Date:** 2026-09-23  \n**Mode:** READ-FIRST → MINIMAL REVERSIBLE CONFIGURATION → LIVE VERIFICATION  \n**Primary Objective:** Make the already-proven Amazon Bedrock Mantle models usable from the GCE terminal/orchestrator with local-file access.\n\n---\n\n# 0. OPERATING INTENT\n\nAmazon Bedrock is being established as a **GCE continuity / bridge compute layer**.\n\nThe practical goal is:\n\n> When Don's direct subscriptions, provider credits, or provider limits for Kimi, GLM, OpenAI/ChatGPT, or other model vendors are unavailable or constrained, the GCE terminal/orchestrator can route work through Amazon Bedrock while preserving access to Don's local files, repositories, shell, and existing GCE tooling.\n\nThis is **not** an AWS architecture redesign.\n\nThis is **not** a framework governance task.\n\nThis is **not** a Nova repair mission.\n\nThis is a narrow integration mission:\n\n> Wire a reversible local terminal consumer to the verified Bedrock Mantle endpoint, prove local-file use through a Bedrock model, expose a small set of verified model aliases, and stop.\n\n---\n\n# 1. AUTHORITY / SEAT BOUNDARIES\n\nPreserve:\n\n**IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL**\n\n**MODEL != SEAT**\n\nRuntime models may occupy technical execution lanes, but model choice does not alter seat authority.\n\nRelevant seats:\n\n- Don — final authority\n- Coda — strategic advisor / governance / reconciliation\n- Nico — implementation / build\n- Luce — verification / ground truth\n- Talon — routing / operational sequencing\n- Keel — deployment / operational stability if later needed\n\nDo not rewrite seat doctrine.\n\nDo not invent new roles.\n\nDo not promote model-specific behavior into governance.\n\n---\n\n# 2. VERIFIED BEDROCK GROUND TRUTH\n\nThe following is already verified and should be treated as implementation input, not reopened unless the local environment contradicts it.\n\n## AWS identity\n\nAccount:\n\n```text\n280768229421\n```\n\nIAM principal:\n\n```text\narn:aws:iam::280768229421:user/PeteW\n```\n\nPeteW inherits:\n\n```text\nAdministratorAccess\n```\n\nthrough IAM group:\n\n```text\nGCE\n```\n\nPermissions boundary:\n\n```text\nnull\n```\n\nDo not modify IAM.\n\n---\n\n## Working region\n\n```text\nus-east-2\n```\n\n---\n\n## Working endpoint\n\n```text\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\n---\n\n## Working credential source\n\nEnvironment variable:\n\n```text\nAWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n```\n\nThe value exists locally.\n\nNever print it.\n\nNever persist it into a new plaintext file.\n\nNever copy it into source control.\n\n---\n\n## Proven authentication behavior\n\nOpenAI-compatible auth succeeds when the existing Bedrock bearer key is presented as:\n\n```text\nAuthorization: Bearer <AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK>\n```\n\nEquivalent OpenAI-style environment mapping used successfully:\n\n```text\nOPENAI_API_KEY=$AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\nOPENAI_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\nDo not expose secret values.\n\n---\n\n# 3. VERIFIED LIVE MODEL STATE\n\nLuce independently verified live 200-OK Mantle inference in `us-east-2` for the following core models:\n\n```text\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2-thinking\n\nzai.glm-5\nzai.glm-4.7\nzai.glm-4.7-flash\nzai.glm-4.6\n\ndeepseek.v3.2\ndeepseek.v3.1\n\nqwen.qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct\nqwen.qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct\nqwen.qwen3-coder-next\nqwen.qwen3-235b-a22b-2507\n\nminimax.minimax-m2.5\n```\n\nKimi K2.5 was separately proven with a live completion:\n\n```text\nmodel: moonshotai.kimi-k2.5\nservice_tier: default\nprompt_tokens: 35\ncompletion_tokens: 5\ntotal_tokens: 40\n```\n\nDo not retest every model.\n\nUse the proven set.\n\n---\n\n# 4. VERIFIED MODEL INVENTORY — VISIBLE ON MANTLE\n\nThe live Mantle `/models` endpoint showed these models as available:\n\n```text\nanthropic.claude-haiku-4-5\n\ndeepseek.v3.1\ndeepseek.v3.2\n\ngoogle.gemma-3-12b-it\ngoogle.gemma-3-27b-it\ngoogle.gemma-3-4b-it\ngoogle.gemma-4-26b-a4b\ngoogle.gemma-4-31b\ngoogle.gemma-4-e2b\n\nminimax.minimax-m2\nminimax.minimax-m2.1\nminimax.minimax-m2.5\n\nmistral.devstral-2-123b\nmistral.magistral-small-2509\nmistral.ministral-3-14b-instruct\nmistral.ministral-3-3b-instruct\nmistral.ministral-3-8b-instruct\nmistral.mistral-large-3-675b-instruct\nmistral.voxtral-mini-3b-2507\nmistral.voxtral-small-24b-2507\n\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2-thinking\n\nnvidia.nemotron-nano-12b-v2\nnvidia.nemotron-nano-3-30b\nnvidia.nemotron-nano-9b-v2\nnvidia.nemotron-super-3-120b\n\nopenai.gpt-5.4\nopenai.gpt-5.4-2026-03-05\nopenai.gpt-5.5\nopenai.gpt-5.5-2026-04-23\nopenai.gpt-5.6-luna\nopenai.gpt-5.6-sol\nopenai.gpt-5.6-terra\nopenai.gpt-oss-120b\nopenai.gpt-oss-20b\nopenai.gpt-oss-safeguard-120b\nopenai.gpt-oss-safeguard-20b\n\nqwen.qwen3-235b-a22b-2507\nqwen.qwen3-32b\nqwen.qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-instruct\nqwen.qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct\nqwen.qwen3-coder-next\nqwen.qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct\nqwen.qwen3-vl-235b-a22b-instruct\n\nwriter.palmyra-vision-7b\n\nxai.grok-4.3\n\nzai.glm-4.6\nzai.glm-4.7\nzai.glm-4.7-flash\nzai.glm-5\n```\n\nImportant:\n\n**VISIBLE != VERIFIED INVOCABLE**\n\nDo not promote untested inventory entries into default production aliases unless explicitly requested.\n\n---\n\n# 5. KNOWN NON-WORKING / DEFERRED LANES\n\nDo not spend time repairing these during this mission.\n\n## Classic Bedrock Runtime / Nova\n\nClassic:\n\n```text\nConverse\nInvokeModel\n```\n\ncurrently returns:\n\n```text\nValidationException: Operation not allowed\n```\n\nThe account's Nova token-generating Service Quotas in `us-east-2` are currently `0.0` on multiple request/token dimensions.\n\nThis is an **account/runtime quota issue**, not a local integration blocker.\n\nAction item for later:\n\n> Request/enable classic Bedrock Runtime / Nova quotas.\n\nDo not attempt quota changes.\n\nDo not change regions to chase Nova.\n\nDo not change IAM.\n\nDo not change AWS payment settings.\n\n---\n\n## Other currently problematic Mantle models\n\nObserved:\n\n```text\nanthropic.claude-haiku-4-5\n```\n\nVisible but live probe failed HTTP 400.\n\n```text\nopenai.gpt-5.4\nopenai.gpt-5.5\nopenai.gpt-5.6-luna\nopenai.gpt-5.6-terra\n```\n\nVisible but live probes returned HTTP 401 / account access denied.\n\n```text\nxai.grok-4.3\n```\n\nVisible but chat route returned HTTP 400 and response route timed out during Luce's test.\n\nDo not troubleshoot these in this mission.\n\n---\n\n# 6. VERIFIED LOCAL CONFIGURATION FINDINGS\n\nRead these locations first.\n\n## Secret source\n\n```text\n~/.secrets/master-secrets.env\n```\n\nContains:\n\n```text\nAWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n```\n\nDo not print its value.\n\nDo not duplicate it into another plaintext config unless unavoidable and explicitly authorized.\n\nPrefer environment-variable references.\n\n---\n\n## AWS local config\n\n```text\n~/.aws/credentials\n~/.aws/config\n```\n\nVerified region:\n\n```text\nus-east-2\n```\n\n---\n\n## OpenCode current state\n\nRelevant files:\n\n```text\n~/.config/opencode/opencode.json\n~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc\n~/.config/opencode/tui.json\n~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json\n~/.cache/opencode/models.json\n~/.local/state/opencode/model.json\n```\n\nKnown facts:\n\n- `opencode.json` currently contains MCP inbox configuration, not Bedrock provider configuration.\n- `opencode.jsonc` is effectively an empty shell.\n- `tui.json` is keybinding-focused.\n- `auth.json` contains multiple providers, but **amazon-bedrock is not actively authenticated**.\n- `models.json` contains an Amazon Bedrock provider definition and model catalog entry, but this is effectively static/cache metadata rather than a proven working local integration.\n- Current recent model state does not show Bedrock as the selected local runtime.\n\nDo not assume cache/catalog configuration is authoritative.\n\nRead actual provider configuration and current schema before editing.\n\n---\n\n# 7. PRIMARY IMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE\n\nMake **one local terminal consumer** capable of using:\n\n```text\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```text\nAWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n```\n\nand a proven model:\n\n```text\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n```\n\nwhile preserving:\n\n- local filesystem access;\n- local shell/tool access;\n- repository context;\n- GCE orchestration;\n- existing non-Bedrock providers;\n- easy rollback.\n\nThe user should be able to work from terminal against local files using Bedrock as the inference backend.\n\n---\n\n# 8. IMPLEMENTATION PRINCIPLE\n\nThe model itself does **not** need direct machine filesystem permissions.\n\nThe intended architecture is:\n\n```text\nGCE terminal / OpenCode / local agent\n    ↓\nlocal file + shell + repo tooling\n    ↓\ncontext assembled locally\n    ↓\nBedrock Mantle inference\n```\n\nTherefore:\n\n> Local tool/orchestrator owns filesystem access. Bedrock owns inference.\n\nDo not design an AWS-side file-upload system unless required by the local tool.\n\nDo not upload arbitrary GCE repos to S3.\n\nDo not move local data into AWS merely to make the model see files.\n\n---\n\n# 9. PREFERRED IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\n\nProceed in this sequence.\n\n## Phase A — Recon\n\nRead:\n\n1. current OpenCode provider schema;\n2. current OpenCode config;\n3. existing provider-auth mechanisms;\n4. existing model alias/shortcut mechanisms;\n5. any GCE terminal wrapper scripts relevant to Kimi / GLM / model routing;\n6. environment loading for `~/.secrets/master-secrets.env`.\n\nDo not modify yet.\n\nDetermine the **smallest reversible integration point**.\n\nPrefer existing provider abstraction over new bespoke code.\n\n---\n\n## Phase B — Create one Bedrock Mantle provider\n\nUse an OpenAI-compatible custom provider if supported cleanly by the current tool.\n\nDesired logical configuration:\n\n```text\nprovider_name:\naws-bedrock-mantle\n\nbase_url:\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n\napi_key:\nenvironment reference to AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n```\n\nAuth semantics:\n\n```text\nAuthorization: Bearer $AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n```\n\nDo not print the token.\n\nDo not hardcode the token.\n\nDo not create a duplicate secret if avoidable.\n\n---\n\n# 10. INITIAL MODEL ALIASES\n\nAfter Kimi works, expose only the verified core set.\n\nSuggested aliases:\n\n```text\nbk25\n  -> moonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n\nbkthink\n  -> moonshotai.kimi-k2-thinking\n\nbglm5\n  -> zai.glm-5\n\nbglm47\n  -> zai.glm-4.7\n\nbflash\n  -> zai.glm-4.7-flash\n\nbds32\n  -> deepseek.v3.2\n\nbqcoder\n  -> qwen.qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct\n\nbqcnext\n  -> qwen.qwen3-coder-next\n\nbm25\n  -> minimax.minimax-m2.5\n```\n\nAlias names are suggestions.\n\nIf existing local naming conventions conflict, preserve local convention and document the final mapping.\n\nDo not override existing direct-provider shortcuts such as Kimi/GLM shortcuts.\n\nBedrock aliases should be clearly distinguishable.\n\n---\n\n# 11. MODEL / WORKLOAD MAPPING\n\nTreat this as capability routing only.\n\nDo not modify governance.\n\nCurrent verified lane map:\n\n```text\nHeavy reasoning\n  moonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n  moonshotai.kimi-k2-thinking\n\nCoding / build\n  qwen.qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct\n  qwen.qwen3-coder-next\n\nArchitecture / review\n  zai.glm-5\n\nLow-cost utility\n  zai.glm-4.7-flash\n\nVerification\n  deepseek.v3.2\n\nExperimental\n  minimax.minimax-m2.5\n  zai.glm-4.6\n  qwen.qwen3-235b-a22b-2507\n```\n\nDo not auto-route by seat.\n\nDo not infer seat authority from model strength.\n\n---\n\n# 12. COST DISCIPLINE\n\nKnown approximate verified/accepted Mantle rates:\n\n```text\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\ninput  ~$0.60 / 1M\noutput ~$3.00 / 1M\n\nzai.glm-5\ninput  ~$1.00 / 1M\noutput ~$3.20 / 1M\n\ndeepseek.v3.2\ninput  ~$0.62 / 1M\noutput ~$1.85 / 1M\n\nzai.glm-4.7-flash\ninput  ~$0.07 / 1M\noutput ~$0.40 / 1M\n\nzai.glm-4.7\ninput  ~$0.60 / 1M\noutput ~$2.20 / 1M\n```\n\nDo not build complex cost optimization in this mission.\n\nBut preserve the principle:\n\n> Cheap utility work should not default to premium models.\n\n---\n\n# 13. LIVE ACCEPTANCE TEST — REQUIRED\n\nDo not stop at:\n\n```text\nBEDROCK_OK\n```\n\nThe acceptance test must prove:\n\n1. Bedrock inference works through the terminal tool.\n2. The terminal tool can access Don's local files.\n3. The model can reason over file content supplied through the local orchestrator.\n4. No file is modified.\n\nUse one known non-sensitive local GCE text/config/markdown file.\n\nPrefer a file under an existing GCE project or GCE_DON area that is safe to read.\n\nTest prompt:\n\n```text\nREAD-ONLY VERIFICATION.\n\nUse the local terminal/file tools available to you.\n\nRead the specified local file.\n\nReturn:\n1. exact file path used;\n2. first meaningful section heading;\n3. concise summary of that section;\n4. confirmation that no file was modified.\n\nDo not create, edit, rename, move, or delete anything.\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```text\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n```\n\nthrough the new Bedrock Mantle provider.\n\nThe test passes only if:\n\n- local file read succeeds;\n- Bedrock Kimi produces the answer;\n- returned path matches the actual local file;\n- summary matches the source;\n- file hash or timestamp remains unchanged if verification is practical.\n\n---\n\n# 14. SECOND ACCEPTANCE TEST — OPTIONAL BUT PREFERRED\n\nAfter Kimi succeeds, run one cheap lane:\n\n```text\nzai.glm-4.7-flash\n```\n\nagainst the same file or another small file.\n\nPurpose:\n\n> Prove model switching inside the same Bedrock Mantle provider without changing endpoint/auth.\n\nDo not run broad benchmark suites.\n\n---\n\n# 15. DO NOT TOUCH\n\nDo not modify:\n\n- AWS IAM\n- AWS API keys\n- AWS account structure\n- AWS billing\n- AWS payment methods\n- AWS Service Quotas\n- Nova Runtime\n- Framework seat doctrine\n- GCE_ORG governance artifacts\n- unrelated project code\n- `.secrets` values\n- existing direct-provider subscriptions\n- Kimi direct provider integration\n- GLM direct provider integration\n- OpenAI direct provider integration\n\nunless a config-level reference is required for the Bedrock bridge and is explicitly isolated/reversible.\n\n---\n\n# 16. DO NOT DELETE / CLEAN UP YET\n\nLuce identified stale or misleading classic-runtime artifacts such as old Bedrock runtime assumptions.\n\nDo **not** delete them during this mission.\n\nDocument them.\n\nCleanup comes later after the Mantle bridge is proven.\n\n---\n\n# 17. REVERSIBILITY REQUIREMENT\n\nEvery local change must be reversible.\n\nBefore editing a live config:\n\n- identify exact file;\n- preserve current content;\n- create a timestamped backup if appropriate;\n- avoid broad formatting churn;\n- make the smallest possible diff.\n\nDo not regenerate entire configs when a small provider block is sufficient.\n\n---\n\n# 18. SECRET HANDLING\n\nNever return:\n\n```text\nAWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=<actual value>\n```\n\nNever print the full token.\n\nIf confirming presence, return only:\n\n```text\nAWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=PRESENT\n```\n\nOptional:\n\n```text\nlength=<N>\nmasked fingerprint=<safe non-secret fingerprint>\n```\n\nDo not commit secrets to Git.\n\nDo not copy secrets into markdown handoffs.\n\n---\n\n# 19. FAILURE CLASSIFICATION\n\nIf integration fails, classify the failure precisely:\n\n```text\nLOCAL CONFIG\nENVIRONMENT LOADING\nPROVIDER SCHEMA\nAUTH MAPPING\nBASE URL\nMODEL ID\nOPENAI-COMPAT API FORMAT\nLOCAL TOOL / FILE ACCESS\nMODEL RESPONSE\nNETWORK\nAWS MANTLE\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\nDo not reopen AWS IAM unless evidence explicitly shows authentication has regressed.\n\nRemember:\n\nMantle has already been independently verified working.\n\n---\n\n# 20. STOP CONDITIONS\n\nStop and return to Don if:\n\n- provider integration requires a destructive config migration;\n- OpenCode requires replacing existing providers rather than adding one;\n- secret storage would require exposing/copying the bearer token;\n- local file access would require uploading repositories to AWS;\n- the implementation starts touching Framework governance;\n- the only available path requires Nova/classic Bedrock Runtime;\n- AWS starts returning authentication failure against the previously working Mantle endpoint;\n- any step would materially alter IAM, billing, quotas, or account security.\n\nDo not improvise around these boundaries.\n\n---\n\n# 21. REQUIRED RETURN\n\nReturn exactly this structure.\n\n## A. VERDICT\n\n```text\nBEDROCK TERMINAL BRIDGE:\nWORKING / PARTIAL / FAILED\n```\n\n```text\nPRIMARY PROVIDER:\n```\n\n```text\nBASE URL:\n```\n\n```text\nPRIMARY TEST MODEL:\n```\n\n```text\nLOCAL FILE ACCESS:\nWORKING / NOT WORKING\n```\n\n---\n\n## B. FILES READ\n\nList every file inspected.\n\nSeparate:\n\n```text\nREAD ONLY\n```\n\nfrom:\n\n```text\nMODIFIED\n```\n\n---\n\n## C. CHANGES MADE\n\nFor every modified file:\n\n```text\nFILE:\nCHANGE:\nWHY:\nBACKUP:\nREVERSIBLE:\n```\n\n---\n\n## D. PROVIDER CONFIGURATION\n\nReturn sanitized provider configuration.\n\nNever include secret values.\n\nShow:\n\n```text\nprovider name\nbase URL\nenvironment-variable reference\nAPI mode\n```\n\n---\n\n## E. MODEL ALIASES\n\nReturn final alias → model mapping.\n\n---\n\n## F. ACCEPTANCE TEST\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nMODEL:\nLOCAL FILE:\nTASK:\nRESULT:\nFILE MODIFIED?:\nTOKEN / LATENCY DATA IF AVAILABLE:\n```\n\nInclude concise evidence.\n\n---\n\n## G. SECOND MODEL TEST\n\nIf performed:\n\n```text\nMODEL:\nRESULT:\n```\n\n---\n\n## H. FAILURES / LIMITATIONS\n\nOnly evidence-backed findings.\n\n---\n\n## I. DEFERRED ITEMS\n\nMust include:\n\n```text\nClassic Bedrock Runtime / Nova quota remediation\n```\n\nDo not solve it.\n\nAlso list any unverified visible Mantle models that should not yet be relied upon.\n\n---\n\n## J. ROLLBACK\n\nGive the exact rollback procedure.\n\n---\n\n## K. CONTINUITY ANSWER\n\nAnswer:\n\n> If Don's direct Kimi / GLM / OpenAI provider access disappeared right now, can GCE continue terminal-based local-file work through Amazon Bedrock Mantle using the new bridge?\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nYES / PARTIAL / NO\n```\n\nwith evidence.\n\n---\n\n## L. CONFIDENCE\n\nGive a concise percentage based on live evidence.\n\n---\n\n# 22. SUCCESS DEFINITION\n\nThis mission is complete when all of the following are true:\n\n```text\n[ ] Existing AWS bearer secret reused safely\n[ ] Bedrock Mantle provider added locally\n[ ] us-east-2 Mantle endpoint used\n[ ] Kimi K2.5 invoked through the local terminal consumer\n[ ] Terminal/local orchestrator reads a real local GCE file\n[ ] Kimi reasons over that file successfully\n[ ] No source file modified during acceptance test\n[ ] Existing direct providers remain intact\n[ ] At least one additional verified model alias exposed or tested\n[ ] Rollback documented\n[ ] Nova/classic-runtime issue remains isolated and deferred\n```\n\n---\n\n# 23. IMPLEMENTATION DOCTRINE\n\nDo not make this larger than it is.\n\nAWS inference already works.\n\nThe missing piece is local consumption.\n\n**Use the existing orchestrator to provide tools and files.  \nUse Bedrock Mantle only as the inference backend.  \nAdd the smallest reversible bridge.  \nProve it.  \nStop.**\n\n---\n\n# SESSION FOOTER EXPECTATION\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nSTATUS:\nCONFIDENCE:\nOUTCOME:\nFILES MODIFIED:\nPROVIDER ADDED:\nMODELS VERIFIED THROUGH TERMINAL:\nLOCAL FILE TEST:\nOPEN ITEMS:\nDEFERRED:\nROLLBACK:\nDON INPUT NEEDED:\nNEXT ROUTE:\n```\n:::\n\nOne thing I intentionally made explicit in Nico's mission: Luce found that the local stack currently has **no active consumer pointing at Mantle**, despite the API itself being healthy; that's the implementation gap Nico is solving. fileciteturn0file0L69-L87\n\nAnd the acceptance test is based on your actual objective, not an AWS smoke test: **Bedrock model + terminal agent + real local GCE file + no modification**. Luce's own continuity finding was that this single config bridge is what turns Bedrock from latent capability into an operational fallback. fileciteturn0file0L114-L127", "text_chars": 19509, "code_blocks": 55, "links": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1"], "citations": ["https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1"], "path_references": ["auth.json", "models.json", "opencode.json", "tui.json"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0925d16e-f589-4c98-85d6-d750c1d92217", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790217516.592, "updated_at": 1790217539.075913, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "**Okay, we're gonna do a simple audition because Luce's busy. Kimi's out of credits. Which one of these models do you think could build this mantle if I load it with the Nico Bootstrap?** ", "text_chars": 188, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "4a3b1431-d97a-43c9-99e6-d7f6cefc5d9b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790217519.922656, "updated_at": 1790217537.659297, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — for **this specific Nico job**, I’d audition these in this order:\n\n1. **Nemotron 3 Ultra Free** — first pick. This job is mostly **repo inspection + config reasoning + cautious edits + verification**, not raw creative coding. A larger Nemotron agentic model is the best f